# What must never reach a build context rooted at the repository.
#
# Note that compose does not build either service from here: it uses
# "context: ./java-backend" and "context: ./python-voice", and Docker reads
# .dockerignore from the root of the build context — so for those two builds it
# is java-backend/.dockerignore and python-voice/.dockerignore that apply, not
# this file. This one covers a build run from the top of the repository by hand.
# The three are kept in step deliberately; changing one means changing them all.

.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
secrets/
logs/

**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/*.pyc

**/target/
java-backend/.embedded-postgres/
java-backend/.idea/

# The v1 JSON tree is mounted at run time by compose, not built in — and it
# carries example customer records that have no business in an image.
java-backend/data/

docs/
*.md
